      "problem": "Consider the equation $4{x}^{2}+8x-12=0.$ How many distinct real solutions does it have?",
      "worked_solution": "To quickly determine the number of solutions, we can compute the discriminant. We have $a=4,$ $b=8,$ and $c=-12,$ so the discriminant is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(8)^{2}-4(4)(-12) \\\\  & =64+192 \\\\  & =256\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the discriminant is positive $(D>0),$ the equation has two distinct real solutions.",
