      "name": null,
      "problem": "The equation $2{x}^{2}+5x-9=0$ has{{field-1}}\ndistinct real solutions.",
      "worked_solution": "To quickly determine the number of solutions, we can compute the discriminant. We have $a=2,$ $b=5,$ and $c=-9,$ so the discriminant is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-4(2)(-9) \\\\  & =25+72 \\\\  & =97\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the discriminant is positive $(D>0),$ the equation has $2$ distinct real solutions.",
